      <section id="what-admins-see">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">1. What system administrators can see</h2>
        <p>
          System administrators have elevated access to COCOCE's infrastructure for the purpose
          of maintaining, securing, and operating the platform. Their access is limited to
          operational data — never your private credentials.
        </p>
        <p>Administrators can view:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Account metadata:</strong> Email address, registration date, last sign-in timestamp, account status (active, suspended, deleted).</li>
          <li><strong>Store and listing information:</strong> Vendor store details, product listings, catalog entries, and inventory status.</li>
          <li><strong>Order and transaction records:</strong> Order history, payment status, shipping details, and dispute records.</li>
          <li><strong>System logs:</strong> Authentication attempts, API errors, performance metrics, and security events.</li>
          <li><strong>Aggregated analytics:</strong> Platform usage statistics, search trends, and marketplace activity — always in aggregate, never tied to individuals.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="what-admins-cannot" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">2. What system administrators cannot see</h2>
        <div class="bg-brand-light rounded-3xl p-5 md:p-6 border-l-4 border-brand flex items-center gap-4 shadow-sm my-4">
          <i data-lucide="eye-off" class="w-8 h-8 md:w-10 md:h-10 text-brand flex-shrink-0"></i>
          <div class="text-slate-800">
            <strong>Administrators can never view your password, session tokens, or payment card details.</strong>
            These are protected by zero-knowledge architecture and are inaccessible to anyone —
            including COCOCE staff.
          </div>
        </div>
        <p>Specifically, administrators <strong>cannot</strong> see:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Plain-text passwords:</strong> Passwords are hashed with Argon2id and salted. Even admins see only the hash, which cannot be reversed.</li>
          <li><strong>Session tokens:</strong> Active session identifiers are encrypted and inaccessible to administrative tooling.</li>
          <li><strong>Payment credentials:</strong> Card numbers, CVV codes, and full payment details are processed by PCI-compliant partners and never stored on COCOCE servers.</li>
          <li><strong>Private messages:</strong> Any direct communication between buyers and vendors is end-to-end protected and not visible to admins.</li>
          <li><strong>Browsing history outside COCOCE:</strong> We do not track or store your activity on other websites.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="admin-authentication" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">3. Admin authentication</h2>
        <p>
          Administrative accounts are protected by stricter authentication requirements than
          regular user accounts:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Multi-factor authentication (MFA):</strong> Required for all admin accounts, no exceptions.</li>
          <li><strong>Hardware security keys:</strong> Senior administrators use FIDO2 hardware keys for the highest-privilege operations.</li>
          <li><strong>Short session lifetimes:</strong> Admin sessions expire after 15 minutes of inactivity — half the regular user window.</li>
          <li><strong>IP allowlisting:</strong> Admin access is restricted to approved network ranges where feasible.</li>
          <li><strong>Separate credentials:</strong> Admin accounts are completely separate from any personal COCOCE accounts.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="audit-logging" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">4. Audit logging — every action is recorded</h2>
        <p>
          Every administrative action is logged immutably. There is no such thing as an
          untracked admin action on COCOCE.
        </p>
        <p>Each log entry captures:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Who:</strong> The specific admin account that performed the action.</li>
          <li><strong>What:</strong> The exact operation (view, edit, delete, export, etc.).</li>
          <li><strong>When:</strong> A precise timestamp with timezone.</li>
          <li><strong>Where:</strong> The IP address and device fingerprint of the admin.</li>
          <li><strong>Why:</strong> A required justification field for any sensitive operation.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Audit logs are stored in write-once storage, encrypted, and retained for a minimum of
          24 months. They are reviewed regularly by our security team and are available to
          regulators upon lawful request.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="least-privilege" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">5. Least privilege access</h2>
        <p>
          Not all administrators have the same level of access. We follow the principle of
          <strong>least privilege</strong> — each admin is granted only the minimum access
          necessary to perform their specific role.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Tier 1 — Support:</strong> Can view account metadata and assist with basic account issues. Cannot modify listings, orders, or system settings.</li>
          <li><strong>Tier 2 — Operations:</strong> Can manage catalog entries, review disputes, and adjust order status. Cannot access security logs or system configuration.</li>
          <li><strong>Tier 3 — Security:</strong> Can view audit logs, investigate incidents, and suspend accounts. Cannot modify financial records or system code.</li>
          <li><strong>Tier 4 — Infrastructure:</strong> Can deploy code, manage servers, and configure systems. Cannot view user credentials or payment data.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Access is reviewed quarterly, and any admin who changes roles has their access
          immediately adjusted.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="data-handling" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">6. Data handling rules</h2>
        <p>
          Administrators must follow strict data handling rules at all times:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>No personal use:</strong> Admin access may never be used for personal curiosity, competitive research, or any purpose unrelated to COCOCE operations.</li>
          <li><strong>No export without approval:</strong> Exporting user data requires a documented business justification and a second admin's approval.</li>
          <li><strong>No sharing:</strong> Admin access is non-transferable. Credentials may never be shared, even with other admins.</li>
          <li><strong>Immediate reporting:</strong> Any suspected data misuse must be reported to the security team within one hour.</li>
          <li><strong>Confidentiality:</strong> All admins sign a binding confidentiality agreement and undergo annual privacy training.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="breach-response" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">7. Breach &amp; incident response</h2>
        <p>
          If we detect that an admin account has been compromised or misused, we act immediately:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Automatic suspension:</strong> The compromised admin account is locked within seconds of detection.</li>
          <li><strong>Forensic audit:</strong> All actions performed by that account are reviewed in full.</li>
          <li><strong>Affected user notification:</strong> Any user whose data was accessed is notified within 72 hours, in accordance with Rwandan data protection law.</li>
          <li><strong>Regulatory reporting:</strong> The incident is reported to the relevant authorities as required.</li>
          <li><strong>Remediation:</strong> Additional controls are implemented to prevent recurrence.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="your-rights" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">8. Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          As a COCOCE user, you have the right to:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Request an access log:</strong> Ask us who accessed your account data and when.</li>
          <li><strong>Request correction:</strong> Ask us to correct any inaccurate account metadata.</li>
          <li><strong>Request deletion:</strong> Ask us to delete your account and associated data (subject to legal retention requirements).</li>
          <li><strong>Lodge a complaint:</strong> Contact our privacy team or the relevant data protection authority if you believe your data has been mishandled.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To exercise any of these rights, contact us using the details in section 9.
        </p>
      </section>

